  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_033 (scvi_n200, resnet50, multiprofile, transformer, weighted) at 0.7131 acc, showing that multimodal fusion with weighted combination provides a substantial boost over RNA-only multiprofile (0.6530). However, the only image encoder tested in multimodal is resnet50, which alone achieves only 0.208 acc. The stronger imagenet_vit_l (0.227 alone) has not been tested in the multimodal setting. Question: Does a higher-capacity image encoder (imagenet_vit_l vs resnet50) improve multimodal fusion performance when all other design choices are held at their best-known values? This is a clean single-variable comparison (image encoder only) against the current best, isolating the effect of image representation quality on fusion. Why best next experiment: Under a limited budget, resolving whether the image modality's contribution is encoder-dependent or encoder-agnostic is critical. If vit_l helps, it justifies further investment in image quality; if it doesn't, it confirms the image signal is inherently limited and we should focus remaining budget on RNA-side or fusion refinements. This single experiment reduces the most important remaining uncertainty about the multimodal architecture."
